{"text": "TERRI L, WINFREE\nPrairie State College Home Address\nVice President, Community and Economic Development 100 Odyssey Drive\n202 S. Halsted St. Tinley Park, IL 60477\nChicago Heights, IL 60411 708.912.0418\n\ntwinfree@prairiestate.edu ; terriwinfree29@gmail.com\n\noo eeeeeeeeeeeNSsF\u00e9\n\nExperienced Higher Education Administrator\n\nDemonstrated and proven ability of providing leadership and direction in all aspects of higher education.\nVast experience in implementing and administering comprehensive Programs in adult, community and\nbusiness education. Fiscally responsible with proven track record of staying within budget and in\nmeeting financial goals.\n\nACADEMIC PROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE\nVice President, Community and Economic Development, Prairie State College (2007- present)\n\nResponsible for planning, organizing, and implementing a comprehensive Program of adult, continuing,\ncommunity education, and contractual training based on the current and emerging needs of the\nbusiness, industrial, human service, professional, and general adult population of the college district,\nAdditionally | provide leadership for developing curricular, scheduling, and financial support responses\nto identified community needs. | am also responsible for overseeing the conferences and special events,\npublic relations, marketing and communications responsibilities of the college, the support services\narea, and information departments.\n\nAccomplishments as Vice President\n\n\u00a9 Serve on the President\u2019s Cabinet and Administrative Council, 2007 \u2014 Present\nServe as a core team member for a multiple college three year \u201cFund for the Improvement of\nPostsecondary Education\u201d (FIPSE) grant, 2010/2011/2012\nHonored with \u201cThe Linda Morgan Volunteerism Award for the Chicago Southland\u201d, 2013\nServe on 2013-2016 Strategic Planning Committee, 2013\nServed as Chair of administration team for successful support staff union negotiations, 2012\nLed team that developed current on-line registration process for non- credit students\nInitiated the first \u201cAnnual Non-Credit Enrollment Report\u201d, 2010\nLed a cross divisional team in Recruitment and Retention, 2011/2012\nAppointed and served on the Higher Learning Commission Accreditation Committee, 2007/2008\nSuccessfully negotiated support staff union contract, 2010\nSuccessfully negotiated adjunct faculty contract, 2009\nOversee the faculty tenure process for Adult Education, 2007 \u2014 Present\nOversee the curriculum approval process with the Illinois Community College Board for Adult\nEducation courses/ vocational courses and programs, 2007 - Present\n\u00a2 Serve on the Policy/Administration Council, 2007 - Present\n\u00a9 Serve on the Budget Council, 2007 \u2014 Present\n\u00a9 Serve on 2010-2013 Strategic Planning Committee, 2009",
